  "releaseNotes": "New Features:\n- expose state manager diagnostics and options\n  Expose LastFailureKind under both recovery policies and an immutable Options snapshot of each manager's effective configuration. Consumers can inspect classified write and clear failures without provoking another exception or retaining mutable configuration objects.\n  Reset LastFailureKind after successful reads, writes, clears and saves, including no-op saves and read-back recovery which reports success. Failed operations retain their classification, and late completions cannot overwrite the reason for a permanent fence. The outbox continues using activation-wide fencing evidence for its existing reminder policy.\n  Custom IStateManager implementations must expose the two new getters; implementations deriving from StateManagerBase inherit them. Registered handles forward both properties after hydration. Consumer documentation and beta migration notes describe the new contract.",
